% HOW TO USE WITH ZOTERO
% ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
% 1. Install the "Better BibTeX for Zotero" plugin:
%      https://retorque.re/zotero-better-bibtex/
%
% 2. In Zotero: File → Export Library (or right-click a collection)
%      Format:  Better BibTeX
%      ✓ Keep updated  (auto-syncs whenever you add/edit a source)
%      Save as:  references.bib  in this project folder.
%
% 3. Better BibTeX auto-generates citation keys like:
%      watsonMolecularStructure1953
%      rothemundFolding2006
%    Use these keys in your .tex files:  \cite{watsonMolecularStructure1953}
%
% 4. Compile order:
%      pdflatex main  →  biber main  →  pdflatex main  →  pdflatex main
%    Or simply:  latexmk -pdf main
%
% ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
% The entries below are PLACEHOLDERS.  Delete them and let
% Zotero populate this file via auto-export.
